            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p01_c02",
              "mark": "M1",
              "text": "Compute outlier threshold Q3 + 1.5 * IQR = 62 + 1.5 * 14 = 83."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p01_c03",
              "mark": "A1",
              "text": "Conclude 95 > 83, so 95 mm is an outlier."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p02",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p02_c01",
              "mark": "M1",
              "text": "Compare (Q3 - Median) = 62 - 54 = 8 with (Median - Q1) = 54 - 48 = 6."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p02_c02",
              "mark": "A1",
              "text": "Observe that Q3 - Median > Median - Q1 (8 > 6)."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p02_c03",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "Conclude that the distribution is positively skewed (skewed to the right), reinforced by the high outlier at 95 mm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p03",
          "marks": 3,
          "marking_points": [
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p03_c01",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "Explain that Machine A has skewness / an outlier (95 mm), so median and IQR are resistant measures, unlike mean and standard deviation which are distorted by extreme values."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p03_c02",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "Compare central tendency: Machine A has a slightly higher median (54 mm > 53 mm)."
            },
            {
              "criterion_id": "9709_s1_t_representation_of_data_m02_l02_cpq07_p03_c03",
              "mark": "B1",
              "text": "Compare consistency: Machine B has a smaller IQR (8 mm < 14 mm), so Machine B produces more consistent rod lengths."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
